# Keep secrets and build noise out of the image.
#
# The frontend Dockerfile runs `COPY . .` after `npm install`, so anything not
# ignored here ends up in the image. Measured locally, that is:
#   node_modules  ~638 MB   (would be shadowed by the image's own install anyway)
#   .next         ~176 MB   (a stale local build, guaranteed to mislead)
#
# More seriously, a real `.env.local` would be baked into a layer. Deleting it in
# a later RUN does not remove it from image history. `.gitignore` protects the
# repo; it does NOT protect the image.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

# --- Dependencies & build output ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Test artifacts ---
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# --- VCS / tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# --- Docs ---
README.md
